<%--
Cache_Shared_Reference_Serialization_Test

Regression test for the shared (non-circular) reference fix in
local-storage.ts process_for_serialization (commit 91f1bc59).

A component sets this.data.a and this.data.b to the SAME array reference
in on_load(). Before the fix, the `seen` WeakSet tracked every object ever
visited (not just the current ancestor DFS path), so the second occurrence
of the shared array (this.data.b) would be misdetected as a circular
reference and dropped/omitted from serialization. After the fix, `seen`
only tracks the current ancestor path (added on the way down, removed in
a `finally` on the way back up), so a shared reference in a DAG is
serialized independently at each occurrence instead of being treated as
a cycle.
--%>
<Define:Cache_Shared_Reference_Serialization_Test>
  <div class="test-container">
    <h1>Cache Shared Reference Serialization Test</h1>
    <div $sid="mount_point" class="mount-point"></div>
    <div $sid="results" class="results"></div>
  </div>
</Define:Cache_Shared_Reference_Serialization_Test>
